and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. </br>You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Simple Past tense verbs can be regular or irregular. </p> Regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.</p> Irregular verbs change in different ways. </p>For questions in the past, you use the auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">did</span> followed by the verb in the base form, like <span class=\"italic\">Did you ask\u2026?</span> </p><span class=\"strong\">Did</span> is the past form of <span class=\"strong\">to do</span>.</p> For Past Continuous, we add <span class=\"strong\">was/were</span> + verb\u201c<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>\u201d to verbs.</p> Some verbs need a change to the last letter to add \u201c<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>\u201d.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talk\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"talked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were talking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"count\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"counted\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were counting\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"go\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"went\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were going\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"take\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"took\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were taking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"travel\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"traveled\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were traveling\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"buy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were buying\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were thinking\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "I was going through some pictures on my camera and I printed some out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We were watching a group of gazelles when a rhino came out of nowhere!", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "scrapbook", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a book of blank pages for sticking clippings and pictures in", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I make a scrapbook after each trip I take.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you hear in a conversation about photo albums.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "album", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a blank book for keeping pictures or photos ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love old photo albums.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "That's quite something!", "type": "name"}, {"content": "That's very impressive!", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I love the picture of the rhino running! That's quite something!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to count sheep", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to close your eyes and count to help you fall asleep", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I was counting sheep until 2 a.m. last night when I finally fell asleep!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to go through", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to search through or examine in sequence", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I was going through the pictures on my camera and I printed some out.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "out of nowhere", "type": "name"}, {"content": "by surprise; suddenly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The rhino appeared out of nowhere!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Write a short paragraph (8-10 lines) about a favorite memory.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe when it was, where it took place and how old you were.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use comparatives.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the Simple Past and Past Continuous tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your paragraph to your partner.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I write about what I was doing when something happened.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write 8 -10 lines about my favorite memory.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I compare things and feelings.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn5le14ob05re2img06.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le14ob05re2img06.jpg", "time": "100", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: How's the jet lag this morning, Sally? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: It's getting there ... I was counting sheep until 2 a.m. last night when I finally fell asleep!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: You used to do that all the time when you were little!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: That's true, but I wasn't traveling the world as a kid. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Well, you had lots of fun in Cambridge anyway. What are these?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Oh, I was going through the pictures on my camera and I printed some out."}, {"image": "engenn5le14ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "23000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: What do you want to do with them?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I was thinking of making a scrapbook about my trip.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Great idea! I made scrapbooks all the time when I was your age.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: I think you showed them to me! I love the old photo albums too!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Anyway, I want to hear about your travel adventures!"}, {"image": "engenn5le14ob05re2img05.jpg", "time": "40000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Look at this one I took in Namibia. We were watching a group of gazelles when a rhino came out of nowhere!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: That's quite something! Were you scared?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally</span>: Not really. I was taking too many pictures!</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sally's Mom</span>: Haha. Well, they are worth it!"}], "audiosrc": "engenn5le14ob05re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn5le14ob05re2img06.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "I can talk about travel and transportation. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say what I was doing when something else happened.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "Do you take a lot of pictures when you go on holiday?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How do you keep your pictures?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Do you use photo albums? Your computer? Your phone?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Let's make a holiday photo album!", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Sally is going <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">old school</span>! She's making a photo album!", "type